All done. Here's a summary of the revision:

## Changes per feedback item

**1. Panel borders** (`src/ui/renderer.cpp`, `src/ui/panel.cpp`)
- Root cause found by inspecting the renderer: `outline_rounded_rect` drew one point per row with `ceil` insets — discontinuous, jagged corner arcs — and `Panel` stacked `border_thickness` nested outlines on top of the fill.
- `Panel` with an opaque background now draws one clean uniform border ring (border-colored fill + inset background fill); transparent backgrounds (the selected-card glow) draw rounded outlines.
- Outlines now trace the true circle with dense angle steps, deduplicated, with points that land on the straight edges skipped — so the glow ring is continuous with no gaps and no double-blended (brighter) pixels on its semi-transparent color. Fills sample corner arcs at pixel centers.

**2. Volume icon** — replaced with a proper speaker: cabinet, a seam-free flared cone (exact scanline trapezoid — the first attempt with two triangles left a visible diagonal seam), and two sound-wave arcs drawn from renderer primitives.

**3. Selected game's title** — the title now always shows the selected game's name, centered below the center card, sized via `ImageFit::contain` (the old asset was also being squished by a stretched fixed rect and had magenta keying fringes). Titles are clean transparent PNG exports from the existing SVG pipeline (same DejaVu Sans Bold style as the original).
- ⚠️ **Assumption you should review:** only "SUPER MARIO" existed as name data. Since this run couldn't ask, I used the placeholder games' existing identifiers — **STAR** and **CAR** — in the identical style. If you consider that inventing titles, I can drop those two assets and show no title for them instead.

**4. KiddOS wordmark** — no logo asset existed, so I added a restrained "KiddOS" wordmark (same typography pipeline, white, top-center) with its SVG source committed alongside, consistent with the project's `source/*.svg` → `generated/*.bmp|png` practice.

**5. Navigation hints** — subtle strip along the bottom, verified against `docs/INPUT_CONTROLS.md` Kid Mode: ◀▶ BROWSE · Ⓐ SELECT · [START][SELECT] PARENT MENU.

**Artwork note:** the magenta-keyed BMP artwork left pink keying fringes on screen. I exported transparent PNGs from the committed SVG sources (identical content, same sizes) for the home screen; the BMPs remain untouched for the manual game-action rendering path.

## Constraints honored
- Still `ui::Screen` + ScreenManager through the UI library; geometry, colors, carousel positions, selection behavior, and battery indicator unchanged; no mouse/touch; textures remain screen-owned with images detached in the destructor.

## Validation
- Build clean (no warnings), **26/26 CTest pass** — carousel test extended (structure, per-selection title textures, wordmark/hints presence, border & glow continuity, magenta-fringe checks); no existing tests weakened.
- Headless smoke test (`SDL_VIDEODRIVER=dummy`) ran the full window without crashing.
- Committed as `0d803f5 feat(ui): refine home carousel borders, titles, wordmark, and hints` — no milestone runner logs included.

**Visual approval is yours to give** — please run `./build/kiddos` from the repo root and inspect, especially the STAR/CAR title wording.
